10. DECISIONS.md

Create a decision register.

Start with the following decisions.

# Project Decisions

## D001 — Book Type

The book is a free general-audience financial-markets eBook and is not intended to be a formal school textbook.

## D002 — Primary Audience

The primary audience is secondary students in Papua New Guinea and the wider general public.

## D003 — Geographic Approach

Global financial concepts should be explained first where useful, followed by PNG applications and examples.

## D004 — Research Standard

Important PNG statistics must be traceable to reliable sources and must include reference dates.

## D005 — Regulatory Sources

Primary regulatory/government sources should be preferred for legal and regulatory claims.

## D006 — Investment Advice

The book must not provide personalised investment advice or guaranteed investment outcomes.

## D007 — Statistical Discipline

Historical figures, forecasts, estimates, targets and current actuals must be clearly distinguished.

## D008 — Unverified Information

Unverified statistics must not be presented as established facts.

## D009 — AI Roles

ChatGPT is primarily responsible for planning, research analysis, review and quality control.

Claude Code is primarily responsible for repository execution, implementation, testing, organisation and automation.

## D010 — Source of Truth

GitHub is the project source of truth.

## D011 — Handover Separation

Task-specific handovers must not replace or masquerade as permanent project-control documents.

## D012 — Scope Discipline

AI agents must not independently advance the project to a later production stage without an approved task.

Do not invent additional major decisions unless clearly necessary.

